    "body": "## Summary\n\nUnder DP attention, every DP rank launches its own Mooncake client and mounts a global segment. The per-rank segment size was only divided by `tp_size * pp_size`, so with TP4 / DP4 each of the 4 DP ranks mounted the **full** configured `MOONCAKE_GLOBAL_SEGMENT_SIZE`.\n\nThis pinned `dp_size` times the intended host memory. On 8xB200 hosts the HiCache host pool already holds 200 GiB per DP rank, so `MOONCAKE_GLOBAL_SEGMENT_SIZE=400gb` tried to pin 1.6 TB more, and `fi_mr_reg` failed with \"Cannot allocate memory\" (\"Failed to setup Mooncake store\").\n\n## Changes\n\n- `HiCacheStorageConfig`: add a `dp_size` field (defaults to 1).\n- `cache_controller._generate_storage_config`: populate `dp_size` from `parallel.attn_dp_size` when DP attention is enabled, otherwise 1.\n- `mooncake_store.py`: include `dp_size` in `rank_scale_factor`, so the per-rank segment is `global_segment_size // (tp_size * pp_size * dp_size)`.\n- README: document that the total pinned memory equals the configured `global_segment_size` for DP attention as well.\n\nThe resulting total across all ranks matches the README's documented behavior: total = global segment size.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Verified `dp_size` defaults to 1 when DP attention is disabled, so existing single-instance / TP-only deployments are unchanged.\n- [x] Verified the scaling factor now matches the number of ranks that actually mount a segment (`tp_size * pp_size * dp_size`).\n- [ ] Run a TP4/DP4 HiCache + Mooncake deployment and confirm `master_total_capacity_bytes` equals the configured segment size across all DP ranks.\n\nFixes #46899.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40618548451](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40618548451)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40618548093](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40618548093)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40618548002](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40618548002)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
